<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name      "borg-backup-ui">
<!ENTITY author    "Thorsten Steinberg">
<!ENTITY version   "2026.10.27.2031">
<!ENTITY github    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/borgforge/borg-backup-ui">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "&github;/main/&name;.plg">
<!ENTITY bootdir   "/boot/config/plugins/&name;">
<!ENTITY pkgurl    "&github;/main/releases/&name;-&version;.txz">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&name;"
        Title="Borg Backup UI"
        author="&author;"
        version="&version;"
        launch="Settings/borg-backup-ui"
        pluginURL="&pluginURL;"
        description="Web UI for Borg Backup – Dashboard, Jobs, Storage, History, Restore Tests and Settings. No pip required, pure Python 3."
        icon="plugin-icon.png">

<CHANGES>
<![CDATA[
###2026.10.27.2031###
### Migration and compatibility

- **Test-channel baseline:** Return to the current main implementation after the PR #595 preview. The experimental sequential Docker backup option is no longer included; existing archive files are not removed by the update. (#597)

### Bug Fixes

- Keep the preceding restore verification outcome and its original expiry after a cancelled test. Show the latest cancelled attempt separately in Jobs, saved status details and test planning; retain report history and do not revive older success over a later failure. Existing cancellation reports are handled too. (#609)
- Handle filesystem access errors when probing a restore-test repository, including USB devices disconnected without unmounting. Record an unavailable result with mount/device guidance instead of a traceback, and leave subsequent checks untested. (#612)
- Hide previous outcome messages while a job is running, keeping their complete text accessible under Show status. (#613)
- Keep job card widths stable when opening live logs; long log lines scroll horizontally within the log viewer. (#613)

### Improvements

- Show live host CPU, available RAM and active runs on the dashboard, with a ten-minute resource history and protected restore-test consumption versus its RAM limit. (#602)
- Use wider resource charts with a subtle fading area and clearer expanded plots, matching the dashboard design preview. (#602)
- Read current values, labeled scales and timestamped samples directly in expanded resource charts with pointer, touch or keyboard navigation. (#602)
- Identify running restore tests directly in the job plan and stop them with the red Cancel button. Cancellation stops the selected run, cleans up its processes and resources, and records interrupted verification. Parallel tests remain independent; cancelling an interval batch also stops its remaining tests. (#605)
- Replace the duplicate dashboard job inventory with a management overview: location-scoped latest outcomes, restore coverage, active runs, actionable problems, 7/30/90-day run statistics, measured repository storage and location totals. Shared repositories count once; missing measurements remain unknown. (#607)
- Add an independent inline saved-status section to Jobs with storage, check, restore and archive details. Show complete saved failure/warning messages directly in each card while retaining the existing workflow timeline and run details. (#607)
- Place server metrics directly below the latest-backup summary row, with server history and active restore-test resource details across the full dashboard width, with CPU and RAM side by side on wide screens. (#607)

- Keep dashboard trends and location totals stable during background refresh and hide locations without jobs from the dashboard table and filter. (#607)
- Hide empty destinations from the Jobs sidebar and return to All locations when the selected destination loses its last job. (#610)
- Simplify Restore Tests planning to four columns with compact counts, inline result labels, an action menu, and collapsible guidance. Keep start/cancel and schedule editing available. (#610)
- Present successful reports as scoped restoration evidence with cumulative L1, L1 + L2 and L1 + L2 + L3 checks. Keep test attempts separate from evidence validity and link cancelled attempts to existing valid evidence. Preserve report filters, technical details, and retained reports. (#610)
- Consolidate technical evidence into one expandable section, attach supporting data to each check and remove the repeated report ID/start/end execution block. Use thin separators and the normal report surface for technical fields. (#610)
- Combine coverage percentage and its file-count basis in one report row so execution and test scope have a balanced five-row layout. (#610)
- Group Restore Tests planning by non-empty locations with the shared location icons and job counts, keeping four columns and removing repeated location labels below job names. (#610)
- Show Edit plan in a floating action menu matching Jobs, with a pencil icon and no row-height jump. (#610)
- Use occupied locations instead of a duplicate job list in the Restore Tests sidebar. Show configured job icons and colors in planning and report rows. (#610)
- Fit the dashboard overview into a compact desktop layout with four summary cards, an integrated location filter, expandable attention details and chart explanations, and a compact location table. Small screens and expanded details remain scrollable. (#615)

###2026.10.26.1618###
### Migration and compatibility

- Restore Tests default to a 2048 MiB memory budget and a 1024 MiB host reserve, including existing installations. Protected tests require a writable cgroup v2 memory controller with cgroup.kill and permission to protect the idle keeper from OOM killing and fail with a clear report if enforcement is unavailable. Setting the memory limit to 0 explicitly disables protection, the reserve check and sequential execution. No backup data or existing configuration is overwritten. (#599)

### Bug Fixes

- Keep the Restore Test memory group alive until final counters are checked, preventing false failures when Unraid automatically removes empty groups after worker exit. Missing final memory counters still fail verification, and cleanup errors no longer hide the original failure. (#599)
- Reduce Restore Test memory consumption for archives with millions of files by streaming file lists while preserving full L2 verification and existing sampling rules. (#599)
- Report timed-out full dry-runs and failed metadata checks as failures instead of successful verification. (#599)

### Improvements

- Add configurable Restore Test memory protection covering the worker and Borg children, monitored host headroom, and sequential execution of protected tests. Preserve per-run reports and log references after retries. (#599)

###2026.10.24.1534###
### Bug Fixes

- Show database exports as an active job step with elapsed time and retain their outcomes in run details. Match template and managed-script selection cards to Own scripts, with themed content surfaces and neutral headers. (#591)

- Allow normal Unraid pool ownership and permissions for database dump storage while keeping dump directories private. Anchor file access against path replacement and report specific storage errors. (#591)

### Improvements

- **Dashboard overview:** Two circular summaries show the latest backup outcomes and restore evidence, with overdue backups and jobs without a restore test plan listed separately. Needs attention links errors, warnings and missed backups to expandable job details. Location groups, job icons and archive names remain visible; repository sizes stay in the overview and complete storage, Borg-check and restore information is available under Details. Empty locations are hidden. (#589)
- Use application dialogs for database confirmations, clarify that local cleanup leaves Borg archives unchanged, and explain that local backup runs include retained job/test dumps across profiles, not Borg archives. (#591)

- Name new database dump folders and Borg archives without UUID suffixes. Keep existing backups readable. Store database Secrets under readable profile/version names with connection metadata; migrate current references at startup while preserving old credentials for recovery. Existing names are never overwritten. (#591)

- Keep job workflow steps in a single row, with horizontal scrolling when space is limited and keyboard access to the full sequence. (#591)

- Select script templates and managed helpers from a dropdown with Description/Source code tabs. Keep large folder and database profile selections manageable in the job wizard with separate tabs, selection counts and scrollable lists. (#591)

- Add reusable MariaDB and PostgreSQL Docker backup profiles, connection checks and cancellable test dumps under Settings. Jobs can archive database exports together with files or on their own, with artifact readback verification and explicit local retention. (#591)
- Ship managed database export scripts with clear update-ownership notices; preserve profiles and custom scripts during plugin updates. Document credential-file setup, backup scope and isolated restoration. (#591)
- Manage database credentials in plugin Secrets, discover selectable databases, and show bundled helpers read-only under Scripts. Align database settings with the shared themed Settings cards. (#591)
- Clearly distinguish editable script templates from plugin-managed database helpers. Browse both with syntax highlighting and line numbers, create independent custom copies from templates, and select Docker containers from a visible dropdown. (#591)

- Add detailed script descriptions and separate description and source cards. Name database backup folders by profile and time, compress new local dumps while streaming, and display compressed/original sizes. Existing dumps remain unchanged; decompress new gzip files before restoration. (#591)

- Match script headings to the neutral Settings style. Offer four general hook templates; MariaDB/PostgreSQL exports remain available through managed database profiles. (#591)
- Add MySQL/InnoDB online backups alongside MariaDB and PostgreSQL. Remove MongoDB, Redis and SQLite from the previous test candidate; preserve existing profiles, Secrets and backups and flag unavailable job assignments. (#593)
- Show the three managed database helpers with detailed bilingual descriptions and syntax highlighting. Existing MariaDB/PostgreSQL profiles and backups remain supported. (#593)
- Automatically remove confirmed completed database operation/test metadata after 30 days. Keep running, unresolved, malformed and unidentifiable records; clean only journal-linked discovery leftovers. Dumps, Secrets and Borg archives are unaffected. (#593)
- Use the application dialog when leaving unsaved database settings. (#591, #593)

]]>
</CHANGES>

<!--
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Step 1 – Download and install the plugin package
  The .txz contains:
    /boot/config/plugins/borg-backup-ui/      → App files (persistent on flash)
    /etc/rc.d/rc.borg_backup_ui               → Start/stop script
    /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/borg-backup-ui/ → Unraid plugin metadata
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-->
<!-- BEGIN borg-backup-ui package installer -->
<FILE Name="/tmp/borg-backup-ui-package-install-&version;.sh" Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
#!/bin/bash
set -e

NAME="borg-backup-ui"
VERSION="&version;"
PACKAGE_INSTALL_SCRIPT="/tmp/borg-backup-ui-package-install-${VERSION}.sh"
PLUGIN_DIR="/boot/config/plugins/${NAME}"
PACKAGE_FILE="${PLUGIN_DIR}/${NAME}-${VERSION}.txz"
PACKAGE_TMP="${PACKAGE_FILE}.tmp"
PACKAGE_URL="&pkgurl;"
EXPECTED_MD5="6dac893486811eaf99a42958bc39c588"
INSTALLED_MD5_FILE="${PLUGIN_DIR}/.installed-package-md5"
VENDOR_DIR="${PLUGIN_DIR}/runtime/vendor"
VENDOR_BUNDLE_DIR="${PLUGIN_DIR}/runtime/vendor-bundles"
VENDOR_META="${VENDOR_BUNDLE_DIR}/apprise-vendor.json"
VENDOR_MARKER="${VENDOR_DIR}/.apprise-vendor.json"
VENDOR_TMP="${PLUGIN_DIR}/runtime/vendor.tmp.$$"

cleanup_package_install_script() {
  rm -f "${PACKAGE_INSTALL_SCRIPT}" 2>/dev/null || true
}
trap cleanup_package_install_script EXIT

file_md5() {
  if command -v md5sum >/dev/null 2>/dev/null; then
    md5sum "$1" | awk '{print $1}'
  else
    md5 -q "$1"
  fi
}

file_sha256() {
  if command -v sha256sum >/dev/null 2>/dev/null; then
    sha256sum "$1" | awk '{print $1}'
  else
    shasum -a 256 "$1" | awk '{print $1}'
  fi
}

json_value() {
  _json_file="$1"
  _json_key="$2"
  sed -n 's/^[[:space:]]*"'"${_json_key}"'"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*"\([^"]*\)".*/\1/p' "${_json_file}" | head -n 1
}

package_registered() {
  for _package_log in "/var/log/packages/${NAME}-${VERSION}"*; do
    if [ -e "${_package_log}" ]; then
      return 0
    fi
  done
  return 1
}

core_payload_present() {
  [ -f "${PLUGIN_DIR}/borg_backup_ui.py" ] || return 1
  [ -f "/etc/rc.d/rc.borg_backup_ui" ] || return 1
  return 0
}

app_payload_version_matches() {
  [ -f "${PLUGIN_DIR}/borg_backup_ui.py" ] || return 1
  grep -F -q "APP_VERSION = \"${VERSION}\"" "${PLUGIN_DIR}/borg_backup_ui.py" 2>/dev/null
}

package_payload_present() {
  core_payload_present || return 1
  app_payload_version_matches || return 1
  [ -f "${VENDOR_META}" ] || return 1
  return 0
}

vendor_ready() {
  [ -f "${VENDOR_META}" ] || return 1
  [ -f "${VENDOR_MARKER}" ] || return 1
  [ -f "${VENDOR_DIR}/apprise/__init__.py" ] || return 1
  expected_version="$(json_value "${VENDOR_META}" version)"
  expected_sha="$(json_value "${VENDOR_META}" sha256)"
  marker_version="$(json_value "${VENDOR_MARKER}" version)"
  marker_sha="$(json_value "${VENDOR_MARKER}" sha256)"
  [ -n "${expected_version}" ] || return 1
  [ -n "${expected_sha}" ] || return 1
  [ "${expected_version}" = "${marker_version}" ] || return 1
  [ "${expected_sha}" = "${marker_sha}" ] || return 1
  return 0
}

ensure_apprise_vendor() {
  if vendor_ready; then
    echo "Borg Backup UI: Apprise runtime is unchanged, skipping extraction."
    return 0
  fi

  if [ ! -f "${VENDOR_META}" ]; then
    echo "ERROR: Apprise vendor metadata is missing: ${VENDOR_META}"
    return 1
  fi

  bundle_name="$(json_value "${VENDOR_META}" bundle)"
  expected_sha="$(json_value "${VENDOR_META}" sha256)"
  expected_version="$(json_value "${VENDOR_META}" version)"
  if [ -z "${bundle_name}" ] || [ -z "${expected_sha}" ] || [ -z "${expected_version}" ]; then
    echo "ERROR: Apprise vendor metadata is incomplete."
    return 1
  fi

  bundle_path="${VENDOR_BUNDLE_DIR}/${bundle_name}"
  if [ ! -f "${bundle_path}" ]; then
    echo "ERROR: Apprise vendor bundle is missing: ${bundle_path}"
    return 1
  fi

  actual_sha="$(file_sha256 "${bundle_path}")"
  if [ "${actual_sha}" != "${expected_sha}" ]; then
    echo "ERROR: Apprise vendor bundle SHA256 does not match."
    echo "  expected: ${expected_sha}"
    echo "  actual  : ${actual_sha}"
    return 1
  fi

  echo "Borg Backup UI: extracting Apprise runtime ${expected_version}..."
  rm -rf "${VENDOR_TMP}" 2>/dev/null || true
  mkdir -p "${VENDOR_TMP}"
  tar -xf "${bundle_path}" -C "${VENDOR_TMP}"
  if [ ! -f "${VENDOR_TMP}/apprise/__init__.py" ]; then
    echo "ERROR: Apprise vendor bundle does not contain a runnable runtime."
    rm -rf "${VENDOR_TMP}" 2>/dev/null || true
    return 1
  fi
  rm -rf "${VENDOR_DIR}" 2>/dev/null || true
  mv "${VENDOR_TMP}" "${VENDOR_DIR}"
  cp "${VENDOR_META}" "${VENDOR_MARKER}"
}

download_package() {
  echo "Borg Backup UI: downloading package ${VERSION}..."
  rm -f "${PACKAGE_TMP}"
  if command -v curl >/dev/null 2>/dev/null; then
    curl -fL --retry 3 --connect-timeout 20 -o "${PACKAGE_TMP}" "${PACKAGE_URL}"
  elif command -v wget >/dev/null 2>/dev/null; then
    wget -O "${PACKAGE_TMP}" "${PACKAGE_URL}"
  else
    echo "ERROR: Neither curl nor wget is available, cannot download package."
    return 1
  fi

  actual_md5="$(file_md5 "${PACKAGE_TMP}")"
  if [ "${actual_md5}" != "${EXPECTED_MD5}" ]; then
    echo "ERROR: Package MD5 does not match."
    echo "  expected: ${EXPECTED_MD5}"
    echo "  actual  : ${actual_md5}"
    rm -f "${PACKAGE_TMP}"
    return 1
  fi
  mv -f "${PACKAGE_TMP}" "${PACKAGE_FILE}"
}

ensure_package_file() {
  if [ -f "${PACKAGE_FILE}" ]; then
    actual_md5="$(file_md5 "${PACKAGE_FILE}")"
    if [ "${actual_md5}" = "${EXPECTED_MD5}" ]; then
      echo "Borg Backup UI: existing package matches MD5, skipping download."
      return 0
    fi
    echo "Borg Backup UI: local package has a different MD5, downloading again."
  fi
  download_package
}

extract_package_payload() {
  _reason="$1"
  ensure_package_file
  echo "Borg Backup UI: ${_reason}"
  tar -xf "${PACKAGE_FILE}" -C /
}

mkdir -p "${PLUGIN_DIR}"

if package_registered; then
  if ! core_payload_present; then
    extract_package_payload "package is registered but plugin files are missing; extracting payload again."
  elif ! app_payload_version_matches; then
    extract_package_payload "installed payload version differs from ${VERSION}; extracting payload again."
  elif [ ! -f "${VENDOR_META}" ]; then
    extract_package_payload "package is registered but Apprise vendor metadata is missing; extracting payload again."
  fi

  if package_payload_present; then
    marker_md5="$(cat "${INSTALLED_MD5_FILE}" 2>/dev/null || true)"
    if [ "${marker_md5}" = "${EXPECTED_MD5}" ]; then
      ensure_apprise_vendor
      echo "Borg Backup UI: version ${VERSION} is already installed, skipping package installation."
      exit 0
    fi
    if [ -f "${PACKAGE_FILE}" ]; then
      actual_md5="$(file_md5 "${PACKAGE_FILE}")"
      if [ "${actual_md5}" = "${EXPECTED_MD5}" ]; then
        ensure_apprise_vendor
        echo "Borg Backup UI: version ${VERSION} is already installed, updating MD5 marker."
        echo "${EXPECTED_MD5}" > "${INSTALLED_MD5_FILE}" 2>/dev/null || true
        exit 0
      fi
    else
      echo "Borg Backup UI: version ${VERSION} is already installed, no download or extraction needed."
      ensure_apprise_vendor
      echo "${EXPECTED_MD5}" > "${INSTALLED_MD5_FILE}" 2>/dev/null || true
      exit 0
    fi
  fi
fi

ensure_package_file
echo "Borg Backup UI: installing package ${VERSION}. This can take a while on USB flash."
upgradepkg --install-new "${PACKAGE_FILE}"
if ! package_payload_present; then
  extract_package_payload "package manager did not extract the full payload; extracting payload directly."
fi
ensure_apprise_vendor
echo "${EXPECTED_MD5}" > "${INSTALLED_MD5_FILE}" 2>/dev/null || true
</INLINE>
</FILE>
<!-- END borg-backup-ui package installer -->

<!--
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Step 2 – Post-install: autostart + initial launch
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-->
<FILE Name="/tmp/borg-backup-ui-install.sh" Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
#!/bin/bash
PLUGIN_DIR="/boot/config/plugins/borg-backup-ui"
PACKAGE_FILE="${PLUGIN_DIR}/borg-backup-ui-&version;.txz"
GO_FILE="/boot/config/go"

# Defensive fallback: some Unraid/plugin-manager upgradepkg runs may finish
# without leaving the package payload in /boot/config/plugins/borg-backup-ui.
if [ ! -f "${PLUGIN_DIR}/borg_backup_ui.py" ]; then
  if [ -f "${PACKAGE_FILE}" ]; then
    echo "Plugin payload missing after upgradepkg; extracting package fallback."
    tar -xf "${PACKAGE_FILE}" -C / 2>/tmp/borg-backup-ui-install-extract.err || true
  fi
fi

if [ ! -f "${PLUGIN_DIR}/borg_backup_ui.py" ]; then
  echo "ERROR: borg-backup-ui payload was not installed from ${PACKAGE_FILE}."
  if [ -s /tmp/borg-backup-ui-install-extract.err ]; then
    cat /tmp/borg-backup-ui-install-extract.err
  fi
  exit 1
fi

# Create default config if none exists yet
if [ ! -f "${PLUGIN_DIR}/borg_backup_ui.conf" ]; then
  cp "${PLUGIN_DIR}/borg_backup_ui.conf.example" \
     "${PLUGIN_DIR}/borg_backup_ui.conf" 2>/dev/null || true
  echo "Created borg_backup_ui.conf from template."
fi

# Clean up legacy Borg Backup UI autostart lines from /boot/config/go.
# The plugin install/boot flow starts the service without persistent go entries.
if [ -f "${GO_FILE}" ]; then
  sed -i '/# Borg Backup UI/d' "${GO_FILE}" 2>/dev/null || true
  sed -i '/rc.borg_backup_ui/d' "${GO_FILE}" 2>/dev/null || true
fi

# Copy restore-test script to scripts/ (if phase-1 migration was done)
# Bootstrap borg-backup runtime directories
BORG_BASE="/boot/config/borg-backup"
mkdir -p "${BORG_BASE}/config/jobs" "${BORG_BASE}/locks" "${BORG_BASE}/scripts"

# Legacy cleanup: old external runtime lib is no longer used.
if [ -d "${BORG_BASE}/lib" ]; then
  rm -rf "${BORG_BASE}/lib" 2>/dev/null || true
fi

# Copy standalone backup.conf.example into runtime config path
cp -f "${PLUGIN_DIR}/runtime/config/backup.conf.example" "${BORG_BASE}/config/backup.conf.example" 2>/dev/null || true
if [ ! -f "${BORG_BASE}/config/backup.conf" ]; then
  cp -f "${BORG_BASE}/config/backup.conf.example" "${BORG_BASE}/config/backup.conf" 2>/dev/null || true
fi

# Copy restore-test script into runtime scripts path
cp -f "${PLUGIN_DIR}/runtime/scripts/borg_restore_test.py"          "${BORG_BASE}/scripts/" 2>/dev/null || true
cp -f "${PLUGIN_DIR}/runtime/scripts/borg_restore_test.description" "${BORG_BASE}/scripts/" 2>/dev/null || true

# Stop any running instance, then start fresh
/etc/rc.d/rc.borg_backup_ui stop 2>/dev/null || true
sleep 1
/etc/rc.d/rc.borg_backup_ui start

# Cleanup local release artifacts: keep current + previous, delete older ones
RELEASE_DIR="${PLUGIN_DIR}"
if [ -d "${RELEASE_DIR}" ]; then
  _keep=0
  ls -1t "${RELEASE_DIR}"/borg-backup-ui-*.txz 2>/dev/null | while IFS= read -r _old; do
    _keep=$((_keep + 1))
    if [ "${_keep}" -gt 2 ]; then
      rm -f "${_old}" 2>/dev/null || true
    fi
  done
fi

rm -f /tmp/borg-backup-ui-install.sh
rm -f /tmp/borg-backup-ui-install-extract.err
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/tmp/borg-backup-ui-remove.sh" Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE>
#!/bin/bash
set -e

NAME="borg-backup-ui"
PLUGIN_DIR="/boot/config/plugins/${NAME}"
EMHTTP_DIR="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/${NAME}"
GO_FILE="/boot/config/go"
RC_SCRIPT="/etc/rc.d/rc.borg_backup_ui"
PIDFILE="/var/run/borg_backup_ui.pid"
WAIT_PIDFILE="/var/run/borg_backup_ui_start_wait.pid"
LOGFILE="/var/log/borg_backup_ui.log"
CLIENT_LOGFILE="/var/log/borg_backup_ui_client.log"

# Stop the service and any delayed start process before deleting payload files.
if [ -x "${RC_SCRIPT}" ]; then
  "${RC_SCRIPT}" stop 2>/dev/null || true
fi

# Remove legacy autostart lines from /boot/config/go.
if [ -f "${GO_FILE}" ]; then
  sed -i '/# Borg Backup UI/d' "${GO_FILE}" 2>/dev/null || true
  sed -i '/rc.borg_backup_ui/d' "${GO_FILE}" 2>/dev/null || true
fi

# Remove runtime files installed outside the persistent plugin directory.
rm -f "${RC_SCRIPT}" 2>/dev/null || true
rm -rf "${EMHTTP_DIR}" 2>/dev/null || true
rm -f "${PIDFILE}" "${WAIT_PIDFILE}" "${LOGFILE}" "${CLIENT_LOGFILE}" 2>/dev/null || true

# Remove plugin-owned payload from the USB flash. User data outside this
# directory, Borg repositories, jobs, histories, and configured data paths are
# intentionally left untouched.
if [ "${PLUGIN_DIR}" = "/boot/config/plugins/${NAME}" ]; then
  if [ -d "${PLUGIN_DIR}" ]; then
    rm -rf "${PLUGIN_DIR}"
  fi
fi

rm -f /tmp/borg-backup-ui-remove.sh
</INLINE>
</FILE>

</PLUGIN>
